From: David Bloomin <452472+daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:35:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui_gateway): update-hold queued prompt survives a long
 drain window; replay lease path covered

Review follow-up on 2f26519116 (t_01a186190e59f122).

- A prompt queued behind the core-update hold is journaled as an update_hold_queue
  turn marker. It was bound by the 15 min turn freshness window, but the drain
  window holds admission up to 15 min and the apply takes 1-4 min more, so a prompt
  queued early was dropped at the post-restart resume (its accept row already
  retired). It now has its own 1 h bound (UPDATE_HOLD_QUEUE_MAX_AGE_S), in both
  session.resume auto-continue and the startup sweep, and joins the sweep's
  update-recovery retry set like core-update pauses.
- Card fix 3 (retry died on session_turn_lease / session_busy): the MacBook log at
  17:44:32 PDT shows "state.db write lock unavailable for 0s" then "session turn
  lease wait timed out" in the same ms, with no holder wait: Desktop admits with
  wait_seconds=0, so a busy state.db was reported as another writer. Fixed by
  7e8e8f4a59 (BUSY_DB_WAIT_SECONDS floor), now on the MacBook (fb393b96b3). New
  test drives the hold-queue replay through the real Desktop lease admission with
  a dead pre-restart lease row and a state.db write lock held past the first
  attempt; it fails if either
  the dead-pid reclaim or the busy-DB floor is removed.
